## The failure
We retained work, but did not reliably surface the Colab behaviour already written in 0036. A fresh-session test accumulated packaging and evaluation work while current Prime still performed the clerical preparation/custody/indexing manually. Its valuable learning risked becoming a pass/fail label instead of an improvement to the working environment.

## The intended effect
Give another intelligence enough context and artifacts to investigate a real uncertainty, while compute handles repetitive structure and evidence bookkeeping. Prime uses the result to improve actual work. This preserves the Director's collaboration and overflow, lets controlled experiments serve the design question, and makes future retrieval possible through affected pages and reasons rather than a long conversation.

## Evidence
October1 Colabs supplied context and specific questions, then Hostile/Overflow/Unprompted. Claude's first broad comparison reported near ties; the second targeted cases exposed repeated instruction failures. The notes on04 retained disagreement and proposed changes without automatic promotion. Scores are archived claims backed by raw prompts/answers, not new reruns.
Current t2 recovered the record meaning well but failed its fixed command policy; automatic memory complicated the input boundary. Both findings matter. SoF's Director-led art/window exploration created useful unplanned design work and required a proper intake path. Their meaning is retained in01 and linked in08.


